From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 01:06:18 +0000
Subject: arm64: dts: allwinner: h616: orangepi-zero2: enable UHS-I timings for
 the SDIO WiFi

SMHC1 carries the UWE5622 WiFi/BT module over SDIO. Per the Zero2 v1.3
schematic its I/O rail (VCC-PG, WIFI-IO) is a fixed 1.8V supply from
BLDO1, which the DT already describes as the 1.8V vqmmc regulator, but
the port only advertises high-speed timing, so the link runs at
50MHz SDR (4-bit) although the controller supports the SDIO 3.0
UHS-I timings at 1.8V.

The vendor BSP device tree for this board enables sd-uhs-sdr50,
sd-uhs-ddr50 and sd-uhs-sdr104 on this port with max-frequency at
150MHz and skips the voltage switch because the rail is already 1.8V.
Do the same here. On a fixed 1.8V rail an SDIO 3.0 card answers with
S18A cleared, so the core skips CMD11 and selects the UHS timing from
the CCCR bus speed bits. If the module reports no UHS modes in its
CCCR, the link stays at high speed as before.

Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---
 .../dts/allwinner/sun50i-h616-orangepi-zero2.dts     | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h616-orangepi-zero2.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h616-orangepi-zero2.dts
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h616-orangepi-zero2.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h616-orangepi-zero2.dts
@@ -37,6 +37,18 @@ &mmc0 {
 	vmmc-supply = <&reg_dcdce>;
 };
 
+&mmc1 {
+	/*
+	 * The SDIO I/O rail (VCC-PG/WIFI-IO) is a fixed 1.8V supply, so the
+	 * UWE5622 is always signalled at 1.8V. The vendor BSP runs this
+	 * port with SDR50/DDR50/SDR104 capped at 150MHz.
+	 */
+	max-frequency = <150000000>;
+	sd-uhs-sdr50;
+	sd-uhs-ddr50;
+	sd-uhs-sdr104;
+};
+
 &r_rsb {
 	status = "okay";
 
-- 
